---
/** Editorial policy -- companion to /about (what the site is) and
 *  /how-we-gather-this (which sources feed it). This page's job is
 *  narrower: what the software shows, leaves out and works out itself,
 *  now that no model-written text is shown (owner 2026-11-05/06). Every
 *  statement here must stay true to the code -- see lib/ai-text.ts. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/site-config';
import { metaDescription } from '../lib/meta-description';

const canonicalUrl = new URL('/editorial-policy/', Astro.site ?? siteConfig.siteUrl).href;
const title = `Editorial Policy — ${siteConfig.siteName}`;
const description = metaDescription('editorial-policy', siteConfig);

const PUBLISHED_DATE = '2026-08-29';

const webPageJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': canonicalUrl,
  url: canonicalUrl,
  name: title,
  description,
  datePublished: PUBLISHED_DATE,
  dateModified: PUBLISHED_DATE,
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: siteConfig.siteName },
};
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <p>{siteConfig.siteName} has no newsroom and writes no news stories. It
    collects public information from the sources listed on
    <a href="/how-we-gather-this/">/how-we-gather-this</a> and shows what they
    publish. No model-written text is shown, and no person reviews an item
    before it appears. This page says what the software does and doesn't do
    in place of that review.</p>

    <h2>What we show, and what we don't</h2>
    <dl class="checks">
      <div class="check">
        <dt>The source's words stay the source's</dt>
        <dd>Meeting agenda items appear exactly as the agenda gives them.
        Events keep the title, date, time and venue the organiser published,
        with a link back. We don't rewrite them.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="check">
        <dt>Status labels come from the source</dt>
        <dd>A meeting is marked Cancelled or Postponed only when the source
        itself says so in a status or notice field. "Free" and age labels
        appear only when the source states them. Where a source gives no
        value, we show nothing rather than guess.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="check">
        <dt>What the software works out</dt>
        <dd>Times are converted to {siteConfig.cityName}'s time zone, duplicates between sources are removed, events are
        sorted into groups from the source's own category or keywords in the
        title, and distances are measured in a straight line from the town
        centre. These are rules, not a model, and they can be wrong; the
        original source is always one click away.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="check">
        <dt>No predictions, no advice</dt>
        <dd>A closure, a vote or a price is reported only once a source has
        published it. We don't say a decision is likely or expected, and
        nothing here tells you when to buy or sell a home.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="check">
        <dt>No arrests, court records, or obituaries</dt>
        <dd>We don't collect arrest, jail-booking or obituary sources. Fire and
        air-quality notices that contain crime wording are held back from the
        page automatically, and a daily check of the pages for Brookings,
        Moreno Valley and Broomfield reports any that slip through.
        {siteConfig.country === 'gb' && 'In Glasgow, an agenda title that appears to name a private individual or a court proceeding is left out; the meeting itself stays.'}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="check">
        <dt>Sources that say no</dt>
        <dd>If a source's robots.txt forbids automated reading, or it blocks
        us, we don't collect from it. We link to it instead and never try to
        get around the block.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Automated checks catch what they're built to catch, not everything.
    If something still gets through wrong, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>
    — see the <a href="/corrections/">corrections log</a> for what's been
    fixed and when.</p>
  </article>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(webPageJsonLd)} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.prose { max-width: 40rem; }
.prose h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
.checks { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; margin: 0; }
.check dt { font-family: var(--font-head); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.0625rem; }
.check dd { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
